{"uid":"30b536ec427d06da","name":"test_validate_subworkflow_hides_target_from_non_member","fullName":"tests.test_routes_workflow_versions#test_validate_subworkflow_hides_target_from_non_member","historyId":"083683cf2908ad4e2f7adacbcabffaec","time":{"start":1793026701018,"stop":1793026701056,"duration":38},"description":"`P2` (isolation closure, item 1's repo-wide sweep): `_enrich_subworkflow_validation`\n    resolved a referenced ``SubworkflowNode``'s target with a bare ``session.get`` --\n    unlike every other place a subworkflow reference is resolved (`workflows/\n    promoter.py::_resolve_version` at publish/run time, `routes/workflows.py::\n    _preflight_subworkflow_node` at deployment-preflight time, both already gated\n    on `get_visible`). A non-member only needs create access to a workflow of\n    their own (a personal one is enough -- `create_version` only checks the\n    *parent* is visible) to embed another project's private ``workflow_id`` in a\n    `SubworkflowNode` and learn, via this validate endpoint, that it exists plus\n    its active deployment's version id/number/status. Now an invisible target\n    reports the identical ``subworkflow_unknown_workflow`` code a genuinely\n    missing one does -- the same \"forbidden is indistinguishable from missing\"\n    contract every other visibility-checked lookup in this codebase holds.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>P2</code> (isolation closure, item 1's repo-wide sweep): <code>_enrich_subworkflow_validation</code><br />\nresolved a referenced <code>SubworkflowNode</code>'s target with a bare <code>session.get</code> --<br />\nunlike every other place a subworkflow reference is resolved (<code>workflows/ promoter.py::_resolve_version</code> at publish/run time, <code>routes/workflows.py:: _preflight_subworkflow_node</code> at deployment-preflight time, both already gated<br />\non <code>get_visible</code>). A non-member only needs create access to a workflow of<br />\ntheir own (a personal one is enough -- <code>create_version</code> only checks the<br />\n<em>parent</em> is visible) to embed another project's private <code>workflow_id</code> in a<br />\n<code>SubworkflowNode</code> and learn, via this validate endpoint, that it exists plus<br />\nits active deployment's version id/number/status. Now an invisible target<br />\nreports the identical <code>subworkflow_unknown_workflow</code> code a genuinely<br />\nmissing one does -- the same &quot;forbidden is indistinguishable from missing&quot;<br />\ncontract every other visibility-checked lookup in this codebase holds.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1793024424136,"stop":1793024424137,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1793024424137,"stop":1793024424137,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_clear_prompt_info_cache","time":{"start":1793026700245,"stop":1793026700245,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1793026700245,"stop":1793026700245,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_dispose_create_app_engines","time":{"start":1793026700245,"stop":1793026700245,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,